From e6c1c96a2fef7ffc5a1f8366b2c71669ebeb8e28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Sun, 5 Jul 2026 12:01:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 31/34] feat(daemon): idle-at-prompt watchdog forces turn
 boundary to drain queued nudges (hq-2kaq)

Persistent agents (deacon, witness, refinery) can land idle at an interactive
prompt after a loop step completes, where queued nudges cannot drain because
they are only picked up at a natural turn boundary. Add a daemon-hosted
watchdog that detects alive + idle-at-prompt + stale (>2min) + pending-nudges
and forces a turn boundary via the proven C-c / clear / continue / Enter
send-keys sequence.

- IsIdleAtPromptWhileStale classifier: stale idle heartbeat, not working/exiting,
  and not in a legitimate await-signal backoff (backoff-until label in the future).
- ForceTurnBoundary + per-session 5min cooldown prevents send-keys storms.
- Complements the v1.2.1 nudge poller (which drains witness/refinery/crew at 10s):
  no-ops when the poller already drained (pending==0); closes the deacon gap the
  poller does not cover.
- SessionStart resume now uses `gt prime --hook` so an interrupted agent
  auto-continues its hooked molecule instead of asking "should I continue?".

Addresses hq-2kaq / gfork-47p.3.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
